=== Migrant hump theorie <section:migrant-hump-theorie>

The modern demographic transition, economic modernization and the process of globalization entailed transitions in migration behavior as well. As countries move up in the Human Development Index, both immigration and outmigration rates are on the rise.

There are no indications so far that the intensity or volume of migration will be on the decline in the foreseeable future. As a result, populations and societies are becoming more diverse, which sets both challenges and opportunities for societies.

In order to make this a win-win situation for as much people as possible, societies need to find out ways to make the reality of migration safe and orderly. Integration in the labor market will be one of the key challenges. What can be concluded from all the evidence so far, is that more societal and economic development will lead to more rather than less migration.

